# Conformance tests vera is known to fail, one test name per line as conform
# prints it (`verilog-a/ch05_analog_behavior/x.va`, `ivtest/ivltests/y.v`),
# with a reason after `#`. `zig build conformance` fails on any FAIL not
# listed here and on any listed test that passes (XPASS): delete its line.
# Seed or refresh it from a run:
#   grep '^FAIL' zig-out/conformance.tsv | cut -f2 > tools/vera.xfail
verilog-a/ch05_analog_behavior/port_access_own_port_inside_instance_rejected.va # VerA now reads an instance port's flow exactly (CHANGELOG "The flow into an instance's port is read exactly", was E0997); the suite's fixture still expects the refusal
verilog-a/ch05_analog_behavior/port_branch_own_port_inside_instance_rejected.va # as above: the port branch's flow is read exactly, no longer E0997
verilog-a/ch05_analog_behavior/port_access_hierarchical_potential_source_rejected.va # as above: a hierarchical port flow through a potential source is read exactly, no longer E0997
